<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  HIVE iOS — PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy

  Satisfies Apple's privacy-manifest requirement (introduced at WWDC23,
  enforced for App Store Connect submissions since 2024-Q2). HIVE ships this
  manifest with:

    NSPrivacyTracking           = false          (ZERO-TELEMETRY)
    NSPrivacyTrackingDomains    = empty array    (no tracking egress)
    NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes = empty array    (no data collected)
    NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes   = empty array    (populated post-archive)

  The three zero-tracking declarations encode HIVE's ZERO-TELEMETRY posture.
  Flipping NSPrivacyTracking to true, adding a tracking domain, or adding a
  collected-data-type is a deliberate policy change, not a routine edit.

  NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes population:
    The array is intentionally empty at v1.0. It is populated with verified
    reason codes per Apple's documented enumeration at
      https://developer.apple.com/documentation/bundleresources/privacy-manifest-files/describing-use-of-required-reason-api
    after the first `xcodebuild archive` + Xcode Organizer Privacy Report
    run observes which required-reason Apple APIs the compiled binary
    actually reaches.

    Any placeholder reason codes are illustrative only and are NOT verified.
    The current Apple codes must be extracted at archive time, and this array
    populated only with codes that (a) exist in Apple's current documented
    enumeration AND (b) correspond to a required-reason API the HIVE binary
    actually uses. Fabricated codes are not permitted — if a dependency would
    require one, it is removed rather than declared with a fabricated code.

    A post-archive CI check verifies coverage and fails on a
    missing-declared-reason for any observed-used API.

  Outbound-traffic envelope (libp2p peers, BYO-CDN, APNS opaque relay, NTP)
  is not tracking.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- HIVE is zero-tracking. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- Empty tracking-domains: no HIVE-owned endpoint is contacted for
         tracking. The outbound-traffic envelope (libp2p peers + BYO-CDN +
         APNS opaque relay + NTP) is not tracking. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <!-- Empty collected-data-types: HIVE does not collect user data
         off-device. All tuple data is P2P-replicated and user-owned. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>

    <!-- Empty at v1.0; populated with verified reason codes per Apple's
         current documented enumeration after the first `xcodebuild archive`
         + Xcode Organizer Privacy Report run. Any placeholder codes are
         illustrative only and must be replaced with codes that exist in
         Apple's current enumeration and match an API the binary actually
         uses (e.g. a DiskSpace reason such as "check disk space before
         write" for a sqlite WAL free-space probe). A post-archive CI check
         verifies coverage against Apple's published reason-code list. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array/>
</dict>
</plist>
